      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Knowledge about Solar Power varied considerably. Some sales persons had simply no idea. Most were not aware of changes in government subsidies and terminology. Financial/performance modelling required closer attention as claims made were often unlikely to be realised within the time lines suggested.All models ignored the ongoing cost of financing a solar power system. That is, they ignored the ongoing financing cost of the initial capital outlay.Finally, contracts/agreements are very much in the favour of the supplier rather than recipiant of the system.",
